00:01:22.364 --> 00:01:23.704
look up Homeroom with Sal,

00:01:23.704 --> 00:01:27.454
it's a slightly modified
version of these live streams.

00:01:27.454 --> 00:01:31.304
So with that, I'm excited
to introduce someone

00:01:31.304 --> 00:01:34.144
who is an expert on all things education,

00:01:34.144 --> 00:01:36.624
someone who I look up to and consider

00:01:36.624 --> 00:01:40.074
to be a good friend,
secretary Arne Duncan,

00:01:40.074 --> 00:01:43.114
former secretary of education
under the Obama administration

00:01:43.114 --> 00:01:44.844
and managing partner of Chicago Cred.

00:01:44.844 --> 00:01:46.257
Arne, thanks for joining us.

00:01:47.124 --> 00:01:48.364
- I'm thrilled to be here inside.

00:01:48.364 --> 00:01:50.984
I just gotta say, just
as a parent, as a dad,

00:01:50.984 --> 00:01:52.644
you've been so helpful to my two kids

00:01:52.644 --> 00:01:54.684
as they were growing up and
just really, really appreciate

00:01:54.684 --> 00:01:56.534
everything you're doing
for millions of kids,

00:01:56.534 --> 00:01:59.044
not just across the country,
but across the planet

00:01:59.044 --> 00:02:01.014
and whatever I can do
to be helpful to you.

00:02:01.014 --> 00:02:03.254
I just wanna be a good teammate

00:02:03.254 --> 00:02:05.304
to your extraordinary work, so thank you.

00:02:06.404 --> 00:02:08.864
- No, thank you, actually,
obviously we've interacted

00:02:08.864 --> 00:02:10.024
many times over the last few years,

00:02:10.024 --> 00:02:12.514
but I just had a flashback
to the first time we met,

00:02:12.514 --> 00:02:14.164
which was on video conference.

00:02:14.164 --> 00:02:15.824
You were secretary of education.

00:02:15.824 --> 00:02:17.664
Khan Academy was like only a year.

00:02:17.664 --> 00:02:21.944
We were on top of a tea shop
and I had a video conference

00:02:21.944 --> 00:02:23.444
with the secretary of education.

00:02:23.444 --> 00:02:25.784
So I put on a jacket, I put on a tie,

00:02:25.784 --> 00:02:27.684
but by the end of the conversation,

00:02:27.684 --> 00:02:29.444
I felt so comfortable
with you that I said,

00:02:29.444 --> 00:02:30.904
and they had stopped recording.

00:02:30.904 --> 00:02:32.624
I said, Arne, can I tell you a secret?

00:02:32.624 --> 00:02:33.457
And, and you said, what?

00:02:33.457 --> 00:02:34.874
And I stood up and I was wearing shorts.

00:02:34.874 --> 00:02:39.874
And so that was all very
present for the COVID world.

00:02:40.884 --> 00:02:42.761
- You've always been ahead of your time.

00:02:42.761 --> 00:02:43.594
(Arne laughing)

00:02:43.594 --> 00:02:44.904
- I've always been ahead of the time.

00:02:44.904 --> 00:02:46.764
I mean, now even shorts I consider formal,

00:02:46.764 --> 00:02:48.429
but I, anyway, we don't have to go.

00:02:48.429 --> 00:02:51.564
(Both laughing)

00:02:51.564 --> 00:02:53.174
So Arne, I mean, maybe
a good place to start.

00:02:53.174 --> 00:02:56.814
I mean, we were obviously,
there's through multiple layers

00:02:56.814 --> 00:02:57.754
of crises going on.

00:02:57.754 --> 00:03:01.071
There's a healthcare crisis,
there's an economic crisis

00:03:01.071 --> 00:03:02.484
and there's an education crisis.

00:03:02.484 --> 00:03:05.494
And I think those really are
where everyone's minds are.

00:03:05.494 --> 00:03:08.594
You've been secretary of education,

00:03:08.594 --> 00:03:13.184
if this pandemic were happening in 2012

00:03:14.264 --> 00:03:17.744
or actually what, even
earlier when in 2010,

00:03:17.744 --> 00:03:20.624
what do you see as the role
for the federal government?

00:03:20.624 --> 00:03:22.404
What do you think needs
to happen to make sure

00:03:22.404 --> 00:03:23.704
that people keep learning?

00:03:24.964 --> 00:03:26.614
- Well, let me just add
to those, unfortunately,

00:03:26.614 --> 00:03:28.914
that long list of crises you talked about,

00:03:28.914 --> 00:03:32.194
I would just add a health
crisis, a public health crisis

00:03:32.194 --> 00:03:35.524
of systemic racism that we are
still trying to reckon with.

00:03:35.524 --> 00:03:39.404
And all the inequities
that we know exist across

00:03:39.404 --> 00:03:41.074
every part of our society,

00:03:41.074 --> 00:03:43.704
education is not exempt from that.

00:03:43.704 --> 00:03:46.064
And systemic racism is part and parcel

00:03:46.064 --> 00:03:48.574
of our educational system
and happy to talk about this.

00:03:48.574 --> 00:03:51.294
So the challenges are many.

00:03:51.294 --> 00:03:52.504
And let me be very clear.

00:03:52.504 --> 00:03:54.684
We made more than our share of mistakes,

00:03:54.684 --> 00:03:57.194
happy to talk about successes,
happy to talk about failures.

00:03:57.194 --> 00:03:59.784
What I can tell you Sal
from the bottom of my heart,

00:03:59.784 --> 00:04:02.114
as we came to work every single day,

00:04:02.114 --> 00:04:04.154
trying to do what was right for children.

00:04:04.154 --> 00:04:05.334
And I would say education

00:04:05.334 --> 00:04:07.744
is the ultimate bipartisan
issue, nonpartisan issue.

00:04:07.744 --> 00:04:10.904
There's nothing political
about more kids having access

00:04:10.904 --> 00:04:13.544
to pre-K and raising high
school graduation rates

00:04:13.544 --> 00:04:15.894
and having more young
people, go on to college

00:04:15.894 --> 00:04:17.904
once they graduate and attracting

00:04:17.904 --> 00:04:20.864
and retaining great teachers
and doing more technologies,

00:04:20.864 --> 00:04:22.294
you've done so well.

00:04:22.294 --> 00:04:24.814
So for me, this has never
ever been about politics.

00:04:24.814 --> 00:04:27.244
It's about policy where I promise you,

00:04:27.244 --> 00:04:29.744
we would have done is
me and my counterpart

00:04:29.744 --> 00:04:32.154
at health and human services
are Kathleen Sebelius,

00:04:32.154 --> 00:04:33.554
who was the former governor of Kansas

00:04:33.554 --> 00:04:35.494
would have been locked at the hip.

00:04:35.494 --> 00:04:37.464
Tom Frieden who ran the CDC.

00:04:37.464 --> 00:04:41.264
Who's a remarkable leader
in the medical space.

00:04:41.264 --> 00:04:43.214
We would have been locked at the hip.

00:04:43.214 --> 00:04:45.444
We would have been very, very transparent

00:04:45.444 --> 00:04:47.294
and open and honest,.

00:04:47.294 --> 00:04:48.944
As you know information.

00:04:48.944 --> 00:04:50.814
We're learning more things every week,

00:04:50.814 --> 00:04:52.594
every day we still are.

00:04:52.594 --> 00:04:55.694
You have to constantly be
communicating with tremendous

00:04:55.694 --> 00:04:57.684
transparency and urgency,

00:04:57.684 --> 00:05:01.014
but also humility to the American public.

00:05:01.014 --> 00:05:01.847
I promise you,

00:05:01.847 --> 00:05:04.504
we would have taken this
extraordinarily seriously.

00:05:04.504 --> 00:05:06.054
I promise you, we wouldn't have buried it

00:05:06.054 --> 00:05:07.294
like the current administration.

00:05:07.294 --> 00:05:09.484
I promise you, we wouldn't
have called it a hoax.

00:05:09.484 --> 00:05:11.484
I promise you, we
wouldn't have put a stigma

00:05:11.484 --> 00:05:13.057
behind wearing mask.

00:05:13.994 --> 00:05:16.234
And it's interesting.

00:05:16.234 --> 00:05:18.514
My focus has always been on educating kids

00:05:18.514 --> 00:05:20.504
and giving them a chance in
life and trying to break cycles

00:05:20.504 --> 00:05:21.944
of poverty through education.

00:05:21.944 --> 00:05:23.284
But this has brought another lens.

00:05:23.284 --> 00:05:26.264
Our first priority, our
first responsibility

00:05:26.264 --> 00:05:28.724
is to keep children and
parents and teachers

00:05:28.724 --> 00:05:31.174
alive and safe and healthy.

00:05:31.174 --> 00:05:32.704
And so that's the framework

00:05:32.704 --> 00:05:36.444
through which we would have
taken on this work every day.

00:05:36.444 --> 00:05:38.911
And I will say, I again,
it's just my heart

00:05:38.911 --> 00:05:40.037
I'm always honest.

